    "Actual results for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025, from the Report of Local Government Finance filed with the Department of Community Affairs (audited figures). Not a budget.",
    "Public schools are run by separate school districts, and Glascock County provides many other services; residents pay the town, the county and the school district.",
    "Covers every fund, including water, sewer, electric, gas, airport and other enterprise funds. Debt service counts long-term principal retired and interest; borrowing and transfers between funds are left out.",
